                                    185+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    186+*/*01* CREATED BY:                                                   */                     
                                    187+*/*     IEAVCVT                                                      */                     
                                    188+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    189+*/*01* DELETED BY: N/A.                                              */                     
                                    190+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    191+*/*01* POINTED TO BY:                                                */                     
                                    192+*/*     FLCCVT field of the PSA data area (location X'10')           */                     
                                    193+*/*     FLCCVT2 field of the PSA data area                           */                     
                                    194+*/*     CVTSMEXT points to the Virtual address storage extension     */                     
                                    195+*/*     OS/VS - OS/VS extention is pointed to by CVTEXT1             */                     
                                    196+*/*     OS/VS1 - OS/VS2 extention is pointed to by CVTEXT2           */                     
                                    197+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    198+*/*01* SERIALIZATION:                                                */                     
                                    199+*/*     Based on the individual fields being referenced.             */                     
                                    200+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    201+*/*01* FUNCTION:                                                     */                     
                                    202+*/*02*  The CVT provides the means by which non-nucleus-resident     */                     
                                    203+*/*     routines may refer to information in the nucleus of the      */                     
                                    204+*/*     control program.  It contains addresses of other control     */                     
                                    205+*/*     blocks and tables used by the control program routines.      */                     
                                    206+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    207+*/*01* METHOD OF ACCESS:                                             */                     
                                    208+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    209+*/*02*  ASM:                                                         */                     
                                    210+*/*      DSECT=YES should be specified on macro call except          */                     
                                    211+*/*      when called by IEAVCVT to create CSECT.                     */                     
                                    212+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    213+*/*      CVT for OS/VS2 is always mapped.                            */                     
                                    214+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    215+*/*      The PREFIX is not mapped unless PREFIX=YES is specified.    */                     
                                    216+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    217+*/*      A USING on CVTMAP or DSECT name will establish              */                     
                                    218+*/*      addressability for all symbols except in the 2 extentions.  */                     
                                    219+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    220+*/*      To establish addressability for the                         */                     
                                    221+*/*      OS - OS/VS common extension, you should code:               */                     i                                    222+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                                                                                               Page    8            
  Active Usings: DEMO1,R12                                                                                                          
  Loc  Object Code    Addr1 Addr2  Stmt   Source Statement                                  HLASM R6.0  2026/10/19 11.13            
                                    223+*/*          L     REG,CVTEXT1                                       */                     
                                    224+*/*          USING CVTXTNT1,REG                                      */                     
                                    225+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    226+*/*      To establish addressability for the OS/VS2                  */                     
                                    227+*/*      common extension, you should code:                          */                     
                                    228+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    229+*/*          L     REG,CVTEXT2                                       */                     
                                    230+*/*          USING CVTXTNT2,REG                                      */                     
                                    231+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    232+*/*      Where REG in either case is any register other than zero.   */                     
                                    233+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    234+*/*      When LISTING is suppressed, you can determine which         */                     
                                    235+*/*      DSECT a symbol is in by using the statement number          */                     
                                    236+*/*      in the DEFN column in the Cross Reference Listing.          */                     
                                    237+*/*      For example, any symbol defined between the                 */                     
                                    238+*/*      statement numbers for CVTXTNT1 and CVTXTNT2 is in           */                     
                                    239+*/*      the OS - OS/VS common extension.                            */                     
                                    240+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    241+*/*      Specify LIST=YES on macro call to obtain a listing.         */                     
                                    242+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    243+*/*02*  PL/AS:                                                       */                     
                                    244+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    245+*/*      DCL CVTPTR PTR.                                             */                     
                                    246+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    247+*/*      Specify %IHALIST='YES' before %INCLUDE to obtain            */                     
                                    248+*/*      the PL/AS listing.                                          */                     
                                    249+*/*                                                                  */                     
                                    250+*/*      For integration, a listing must not be requested unless     */                     
                                    251+*/*      your module creates the CSECT.                              */                     
